A||||1||wkayl||Security update (more personal experience)..||||1||
Z||000000||wkayl||09-17-2001||01:33 AM||||As luck would have it, I had another service call at the airport today.  I had to go to a different part of the airport so I used a different gate. It was a gate that my security card was never authorized to open.  The procedure at this gate calls for me into go into the guard station.  At least here I had to produce a drivers license, inform them who I was going to see, give them a business card, van number, and how long I would be there.  I parked under the main terminal.  My van was never searched.  The closest the guards came to it was looking at it parked 40 ft from the guard station.  It doesn’t give a person a very secure feeling.  I am going to send the information of the last 2 days to my boss and let him make the decision as to how far this information should go.<P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sig_2.jpg">    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/usa1017[1].gif">   <BR>Dnyee's 88 Formula, Casey's 86GT, Wayne's 86GT.  <BR>We consider my wife as being "Fiero Challenged"||||reg||1
Z||000001||thomas_l||09-17-2001||09:32 AM||||When our family were finally returning to Atlanta from Los Angeles, my wife's son got his American Airlines stand-by boarding pass (original flight got canceled before we even got to LAX at 4am) WITHOUT SHOWING ANY ID! I guess since the name he gave matched a reservation and he wasn't wearing a turban they figured he was OK. Oh yeah, at the security stand they checked him - his boarding pass that is.||||reg||8
